Thu – VirtualBox and Kali Linux

VirtualBox can be used to run a virtual computer on my PC. Kali Linux is a Linux OS that can be used for Cybersecurity and Ethical Hacking.
This means I can use hacking tools on my computer.

I can practice hacking in a safe virtual environment.
If anything goes wrong then it will affect the virtual machine mainly.

By typing ‘cat /etc/os-release’ we can see what version of Linux we are running.
This can help me identify what Operating System is installed on Kali.

My previous version of Kali Linux would show up as Inaccessible due to VirtualBox not being able to find the needed files. To fix this I re-downloaded Kali.

VirtualBox requires the files for the VM to run a virtual computer.
The C:\Kali folder should never be deleted as it contains important files for the virtual machine.
Deleting these files can break Kali or cause you to lose your setup.



